// Title: Invoke-Obfuscation Obfuscated IEX Invocation
// ID: 4bf943c6-5146-4273-98dd-e958fd1e3abf
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Daniel Bohannon (@Mandiant/@FireEye), oscd.community
// Date: 2019-11-08
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027, attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
// Description: Detects all variations of obfuscated powershell IEX invocation code generated by Invoke-Obfuscation framework from the following code block
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((CommandLine =~ /\$PSHome\[\s*\d{1,3}\s*\]\s*\+\s*\$PSHome\[/i) or (CommandLine =~ /\$ShellId\[\s*\d{1,3}\s*\]\s*\+\s*\$ShellId\[/i) or (CommandLine =~ /\$env:Public\[\s*\d{1,3}\s*\]\s*\+\s*\$env:Public\[/i) or (CommandLine =~ /\$env:ComSpec\[(?:\s*\d{1,3}\s*,){2}/i) or (CommandLine =~ /\*mdr\*\W\s*\)\.Name/i) or (CommandLine =~ /\$VerbosePreference\.ToString\(/i) or (CommandLine =~ /\[String\]\s*\$VerbosePreference/i))
